# pymcdc writes <source>.mdc NEXT TO the file it analyses. The domain layer must
# stay byte-identical across all five families, so a tool that drops artifacts
# into the source tree has to be contained -- the runner sweeps them into
# reports/ and this rule keeps any stragglers out of git.
*.mdc
reports/
*.log
.DS_Store
# Upstream tool corpora must not live on branch roots — they inflate taxonomy
# evidence (e.g. Test Case Maintenance / git-churn) and are not part of this cell.
Tool Triggering (Tool Github Test data)/
Tool Triggering (Synthetic Data)/
Tool Clean (Synthetic Data)/
Tool Invalid (Synthetic Data)/
